  "numeric_model": "Nearest representative elevation; band boundaries are midpoint heights. Visible elevation bands use nearest-height assignment. Unioned superlevel footprints are painted ascending, with lower fills extending underneath higher fills to avoid transparent antialiasing seams. Convex working pieces are Boolean-unioned per elevation using NonZero fill on the original i64 coordinate grid, preserving holes. One compound SVG path per superlevel footprint removes internal mesh edges; unioned outlines can be concave. Convexity uses exact i128 supporting-line predicates on normalized coordinates quantized to 1e-10 radius units. Only convex clipping primitives are canonicalized after rounding; concave terrain regions and merge candidates are never replaced with hulls. Inclusive elevation filters clip the working mesh before band quantization; excluded areas are transparent. No smoothing.",
  "color_model": "Opaque #RRGGBB colors; rounded 8-bit sRGB channels. Gradient positions span the retained elevation endpoints unless color_range explicitly fixes a scale. Modes: encoded sRGB, linear-light sRGB, HSV shortest/longest hue path, or rainbow stops. Flat terrain uses the lowest color. Every-N patterns count base levels established by levels/interval after exclusion, anchored at the first base level at or above their start; inserted specific levels do not change pattern counting. Last matching pattern wins per attribute, then specific overrides, then no-fill/no-stroke switches. Stroke widths use non-scaling screen pixels and outline unioned elevation boundaries. Legacy gray is the reference grayscale channel, not custom-color luminance; fill is authoritative.",
  "style": {
    "fill": {
      "lowest": "#ffffff",
      "highest": "#000000",
      "mode": "srgb",
      "stops": []
    },
    "stroke": {
      "lowest": "#888888",
      "highest": "#888888",
